{"availability":"available","full":"HaoyiZhu/PointCloudMatters","name":"PointCloudMatters","description":"[NeurIPS 2024 D&B] Point Cloud Matters: Rethinking the Impact of Different Observation Spaces on Robot Learning","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":93,"forks":3,"created":"2024-06-04T09:16:50Z","updated":"2024-10-14T03:54:45Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://haoyizhu.github.io/pcm/","topics":["benchmark","observation-space","point-cloud","robot-learning","robot-manipulation","robotics"],"demo":"https://haoyizhu.github.io/pcm/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:01.089Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:01.089Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:01.089Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T04:52:01.089Z","stars":93,"forks":3}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Haoyi Zhu, Yating Wang, Di Huang, Weicai Ye, Wanli Ouyang, Tong He","This is the official implementation of NeurIPS 2024 D&B track paper \"Point Cloud Matters: Rethinking the Impact of Different Observation Spaces on Robot Learning\". Real-world codes can be found in RealRobot.","In robot learning, the observation space is crucial due to the distinct characteristics of different modalities, which can potentially become a bottleneck alongside policy design. In this study, we explore the influence of various observation spaces on robot learning, focusing on three predominant modalities: RGB, RGB-D, and point cloud. We introduce OBSBench, a benchmark comprising two simulators and 125 tasks, along with standardized pipelines for various encoders and policy baselines. Extensive experiments on diverse contact-rich manipulation tasks reveal a notable trend: point cloud-based…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HaoyiZhu/PointCloudMatters/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d64d8d72efd4419459a46e131ff5ccc9525bab0fa0afb63c37093fbcd56713e3","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:01.331Z"},"overviewChec